<title>USA: Weather threat to ships off Madagascar, North Sea.</title>
<headline>Weather threat to ships off Madagascar, North Sea.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Josie is a threat to shipping as is turns south towards the Mozambique Channel, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cyclone currently has winds of 55 mph which are expected to intensify to 75 mph during the next 36 hours.</p>
<p>Shipping is also under threat in the North Sea and English Channel where westerly winds are strong.</p>
